WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.520
After the Tumu Crisis, the Oirat army approached Beijing, and the capital was filled with panic.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:10.200
The people on the city wall looked at the dust in the distance, their hearts full of unease.

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:15.480
Minister Yu Qian stepped forward, advocating a firm defense of the capital and firmly opposing a move south.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:20.040
Yu Qian's voice was firm and strong, and the ministers gradually quieted down.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:24.920
He organized soldiers and civilians to defend together, repairing the city wall, preparing grain, and standing guard day and night.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:29.760
Everyone worked together, carrying bag after bag of grain up onto the high city wall.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:34.800
The Battle to Defend Beijing began, and the generals and soldiers worked together to repel the Oirat army.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:39.440
Drums thundered on the city wall, and the defenders' banners flew high.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:44.000
The capital finally turned from danger to safety, the people cheered thunderously, and the situation stabilized.

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:48.360
The children clapped happily, and red lanterns were hung in the streets.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:52.800
Yu Qian thus became a famous loyal minister of the Ming dynasty, a national hero admired by all.

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:57.520
The people looked up at Yu Qian on the city wall, their eyes full of gratitude.
